# Line endings are load-bearing in this repository, which is not usually true.
#
# `scripts/build-docs.mjs --check` and `scripts/build.mjs --check` do a *byte*
# comparison: they re-render the docs and recompile the engines in memory and
# fail if what is committed differs. That is the guard that stops a committed
# `.wasm` or `.html` drifting away from the source it claims to be built from.
#
# The builders emit LF. With `core.autocrlf=true` — the Windows default, and
# what this repo was developed under — a checkout hands the working tree CRLF
# instead, so every generated page compares unequal and `npm run check` reports
# all of them stale on a clean clone. Pinning the text formats to LF on
# checkout makes the comparison mean what it says on every platform.
#
# Verified against d194645: before this file existed, `--check` failed on a
# fresh worktree with 20 pages reported stale and nothing actually wrong.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never let a filter near a compiled engine. Git detects these as binary
# anyway, but the committed `.wasm` files are the one thing in here that a
# newline conversion would silently corrupt, so say it explicitly.
*.wasm binary

# Artwork is generated as text by the logo scripts and diffed like text.
*.svg text eol=lf
